@tradition rec-chiefs-talk
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// Wren talks, the chiefs': every 2 weeks on a Thursday 19:00-19:45 (days 18, 32, 46...), in the auditorium seats (house
// lights half up, the speaker on a stool, no lectern; 20 to 40, a gathering). FOR RA: plus the one-off Monday on Day 8
// (Dr. Sato, 'What lives between the stars', talk.sato, after the creature leaves at 18:40); the format has no one-off
// day (year day 8 would repeat every year). The rota: 8 sato talk.sato; 18 calder talk.calder ('The Wren's first refit',
// ends 19:45 before Echo Signal at 20:30); 32 holt; 46 ferreira (talks to come). The speaker is the host (the rota).
k: 495
title: Chief's talk
when: every 2 weeks thursday from day 18
at: 19:00-19:45
min: 30
jitter: 10
where: 7 room Auditorium: rec:seat
hold: none
who: officers 35%, juniors 30%, everyone 25%
anim: everyone talk
from: The Wren talks
flag: rec.on

== mail
- A chief's talk tomorrow, {time} in the auditorium. Twenty-five minutes of their department's best story, then questions. Come and ask one.
== ask
- Chief's talk tonight. The whole department's going. Well, they've been told to.   #funny
- Are you going to the chief's talk? Sit near the front. They notice who asks.
== here
- Shh. The chief's on.
- Good turnout. Look at that.
- Hands up for questions. Go on.
== thanks
- You find a seat as the house lights come half up. The chief sits on a stool at the front of the stage and begins.
== chatter
- The chief's talk was brilliant. I didn't know half of that.   #warm
- Somebody asked a question at the chief's talk and the chief said "good question". Twice.   #funny
- Chiefs' talks every two weeks. I've marked mine on the Calendar.
